One issue: `registerReceiver` on Android 14+ (targetSdk 34+) requires `RECEIVER_EXPORTED`/`RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED` flag for non-system broadcasts. For system broadcasts like ACTION_SCREEN_ON, the flag is not required... Actually, on Android 14 (API 34), `registerReceiver` requires the export flag unless the receiver is registered **only for system broadcasts**. From the docs: "If your app targets Android 14 or higher, you must specify a flag... If you're registering a receiver for system broadcasts only, you can use RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED." Hmm, let me recall precisely.

The Context.registerReceiver overload with flags is required when targeting API 34+... The rule: apps targeting U+ must specify RECEIVER_EXPORTED or RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED when registering receivers for non-system broadcasts. For receivers that only listen to system broadcasts, the flag isn't required (context-registered receivers for protected system broadcasts are exempt).

To be safe, use the 3-arg overload with `Context.RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED` on API 33+ (the constant is `Context.RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED`, available since API 26 for registerReceiver with flags... actually RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED was added in API 33 (Android 13)). So:

```kotlin
if (Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= Build.VERSION_CODES.TIRAMISU) {
    registerReceiver(screenReceiver, filter, Context.RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED)
} else {
    registerReceiver(screenReceiver, filter)
}
```

